There are also four text fields: \"Department matches record\", \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\", and two empty fields.\n\n**Summary:**\nThe image shows a screenshot of the CoreID Admin Console, with a form for identity verification.\n\n**Detailed Description:**\n\n* The application is the CoreID Admin Console.\n* The current screen is a form for identity verification.\n* The overall layout is a simple form with checkboxes and text fields.\n* The form has two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n* There are four text fields: \"Department matches record\", \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\", and two empty fields.\n\n**Extracted Text:**\nNone\n\n**Errors and Warnings:**\nNone visible\n\n**Likely Issue Category and Severity:**\nUnknown\n\n**Observed Facts vs Inference:**\n\n* OBSERVED FACTS:\n\t+ The form is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n\t+ There are two checkboxes and four text fields.\n\t+ The form has a white background and a dark blue sidebar.\n* INFERENCE:\n\t+ The form is likely used for employee identity verification.\n\t+ The checkboxes and text fields may be used to collect information about the employee's identity.\n\n**Confidence Score and Notes:**\nCONFIDENCE SCORE: 0.8\nCONFIDENCE LEVEL: Medium\nCONFIDENCE REASON: The image is clear, but the text fields are empty, which makes it difficult to determine the exact purpose of the form.\n\nStep 4: Temporary password issued\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Reset Password\nSelect Generate Temporary Password. Leave Force change at next sign-in checked — this is the default and it must not be disabled.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 4 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.95 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a password reset page for an employee, with a white background and a blue button that says \"Generate Temporary Password\". The page has a title that reads \"Reset Password - J. Employee\" and a temporary password field with a checkbox to force a change at the next sign-in.\n\n*   **Title**: \"Reset Password - J. Employee\"\n*   **Temporary Password Field**: A field to enter a temporary password, with a checkbox to force a change at the next sign-in.\n*   **Generate Temporary Password Button**: A blue button to generate a temporary password.\n*   **Background**: White\n\n**Extracted Text:**\n\n*   None\n\n**Errors and Warnings:**\n\n*   None visible\n\n**Likely Issue Category and Severity:**\n\n*   Category: Account/authentication\n*   Severity: Medium\n*   Reason: The page is for resetting a password, which is a common issue that requires authentication.\n\n**Observed Facts vs Inference:**\n\n*   **Observed Facts:**\n    *   The page has a title that reads \"Reset Password - J. Employee\".\n    *   There is a temporary password field with a checkbox to force a change at the next sign-in.\n    *   There is a blue button to generate a temporary password.\n    *   The background is white.\n*   **Inference:**\n    *   The user is trying to reset their password, which suggests that they may have forgotten it or are having trouble accessing their account.\n\n**Confidence Score and Notes:**\n\n*   CONFIDENCE SCORE: 0.95\n*   CONFIDENCE LEVEL: High\n*   CONFIDENCE REASON: The image is clear and well-lit, making it easy to read the text and identify the different elements on the page.\n\nStep 5: Temporary password relayed securely\nNavigation: Phone / voice channel — not logged in CoreID\nRead the temporary password to the caller verbally over the verified phone line. Never send it by email, chat, or ticket comment in plain text. See [CISA's guidance on requiring strong passwords](https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world/require-strong-passwords) for the reasoning behind credential-handling policy.\nStep 6: Ticket resolved with audit note\nNavigation: Ticketing system → ticket → Resolution notes\nLog what was done (identity checks matched, temporary password issued, force